# No Tests

Do **not** write, generate, expand, or “complete” tests as part of feature, fix, or refactor work. Product code is done without a test file.

## When

- Default: skip tests entirely
- Allowed only when the user **explicitly** asks for tests in that message (e.g. “schrijf een test”, “add coverage for …”)
- Existing tests: leave them alone unless the user asked to change tests, or a requested code change makes an existing test fail — then update that failing test as little as needed, do not add new cases

## Do not

- Add `*.test.ts` / `*.spec.ts` / `*.test.js` (or Playwright/Cypress files) alongside a change
- Create `src/tests/**` fixtures or helpers “for the new behavior”
- Expand an existing test file with extra `it(...)` / `test(...)` cases
- Offer to write tests, add a “Test plan” of new unit tests, or run a test-writing pass unprompted
- Use tests as a substitute for verifying the actual product change

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — unsolicited tests after a bugfix
it('emits lobby.started only once when log lines repeat', async () => {
	expect(started).toHaveBeenCalledOnce();
});

// ✅ GOOD — ship the fix only; no new test file or extra cases
```
